{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fourth verified instance, and the first caught **before** review rather than after — `cb2b-7446-748c-47bc`, swept against current `origin/main`.\n\nIts AC1 requires `git grep -n '_ALIASES\\b\\|_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES\\|_map_legacy_env' -- src tests scripts` to return empty. It cannot, on any correct implementation. Two independent reasons, both of the class this bug describes:\n\n1. **Regex over-match.** `\\b` anchors the end of the identifier, so `_ALIASES\\b` also matches the tail of unrelated live names: `_ARCH_ALIASES` (`scripts/ensure_pandoc.py:50,94`), `_HIDDEN_ALIASES` and `_REMOVED_SIMPLE_CLI_ALIASES` (`src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:31,64,183,186,190`, `_cli/_registry.py:565`), `_EDIT_FLAG_ALIASES` (`_commands/composer_edit.py:210,388`), `_DEPRECATED_PROVIDER_ALIASES` (`llm/providers.py:32,64`), plus 6 test modules referencing `_HIDDEN_ALIASES`. 19 hits the story must not touch.\n\n2. **Prose the deletion cannot reach.** `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:177` is a docstring narrating that `_env_signature` *used to* read `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` — correct as written and not a defect. `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json` and `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/table.json` contain `_map_legacy_env` inside captured ticket-body prose used as bridge-rendering fixtures; editing them would corrupt the fixtures.\n\nThe same sweep also found that `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` and `_map_legacy_env` are **already absent from `src/`**, so one of the plan's enumerated deletion targets no longer exists — the enumeration is wrong in both directions at once, naming a path with nothing to delete while missing paths that carry hits.\n\nThis instance sharpens the proposed check in two ways the first three did not:\n\n- A grep-shaped AC needs its **regex** validated against the tree, not just its path list. An AC that over-matches is as unsatisfiable as one that under-enumerates, and the failure looks identical at close time.\n- The sweep must distinguish **code references from prose references**. Docstrings recording history and captured-text fixtures legitimately retain a deleted symbol's name forever. A check that flags them as omissions would be noise, so path exclusions (`tests/fixtures`) and a prose/code distinction belong in the design.\n\nBoth reinforce AC1 and AC2 as written rather than changing them; recording here so the implementer has a concrete fixture to build against."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793421219036466786,"uuid":"17233c2a-27d8-4c79-a21e-8f789a63187a"}